  "rationale": "The plant is split into two automata: one for perception (sensors) and one for motion commands. The specification binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed. Forward and random_walk are prioritized in clear states, while obstacle events trigger brief, directed recovery. Full_rotate and move_backward are reserved for last-resort and only reachable via dedicated states. All transitions are deterministic and respect the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to allow modular specification binding.",
    "Specification automata encode safe, progress-maximizing exploration with conservative, minimal recovery and rapid return to forward progress after obstacles clear."
